    "bounding box" : [ 91.801, 252.617, 520.201, 286.491 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Whenever we are working in the Chow ring of a space equipped with a map to BGL2, BG, or B(Gm × Gm), we will denote by αi βi, etc., the pullbacks of these classes from CH∗(BGL2), etc. We have the following explicit presentations of these rings:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 91.801, 223.292, 520.199, 245.21 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lemma 2.4 ([Tot14, Theorem 2.13 and Lemma 2.12; Lar21, Theorem 5.2 and Lemma 7.1]). We have the presentations"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 91.801, 171.984, 522.618, 220.023 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "CH∗(BGL2) ∼= Z[α1,α2], CH∗(BG) ∼= Z[β1,β2,γ]/(2γ,γ2+β1γ), CH∗ B(Gm × Gm) ∼= Z[t1,t2]. Moreover, the norm (or transfer map) from Gm × Gm to G – in other words, the pushforward π∗: CH∗(Gm × Gm) → CH∗(G) along the index 2 inclusion Gm × Gm → G – is given by"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
